---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Disclaimer — Andrew Morrison"
  description="The views expressed on this website are solely those of the author in a personal capacity."
>
  <div class="content-container animate-in">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="section-label">Disclaimer</span>
      <h1>Personal views only</h1>
      <div class="divider"></div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The views expressed on this website are solely those of the author in a personal
        capacity and do not represent the views or positions of any current or former employer,
        affiliated organisation, or professional body.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site is maintained independently for the purposes of personal reflection, idea
        development, and the sharing of lived experience.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ai">How I use generative AI</h2>
      <p>
        I use generative AI tools to help research, draft, and collate the material across
        this site. I treat them as an assistant — for gathering sources, structuring thinking,
        and tidying prose — but the judgement, the editorial decisions, and the responsibility
        for what's published are mine.
      </p>
      <p>
        I think being transparent about this matters, so I'd rather say it plainly here than
        leave it unsaid. The slop-meter at the foot of each post comes from the same instinct:
        an anonymous, low-friction way for you to tell me when something reads more like a
        machine than a person. I read that signal, and I use it to write better.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
.page-header { padding: 4rem 0 1rem; }
.page-header h1 { margin: 0.75rem 0; }
.prose { padding-bottom: 6rem; }
.prose h2 { margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; font-size: 1.5rem; }
/* offset anchor jumps so the heading clears the sticky nav */
.prose h2[id] { scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
</style>
